            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0336" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 183.7/3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-18T13:50:00+00:00"
                            >January 18, 1919—1:50 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>323. [From Lansing.] Your 281 January 17th 4 p.m. There was never any question
                    regarding representation of Roumania at the Peace Conference. With unanimous
                    approval she has been assigned two representatives.</p>
                <p>Same information sent to Vopicka through Embassy here, referring to joint
                    telegram from Allied Ministers Jassy, dated Bucharest January 7th. Lansing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
